<?xml version="1.0"?><quiz type="multichoice" id="1121" lang="E" hascredits="0"><question><text>&lt;html&gt;The rock crawler, a distant relative of crickets, can survive in the freezing temperatures of the Himalayas. How?
&lt;/html&gt;</text><image/><imagerefid/><audio/><audiorefid/></question><answers correct="3"><answer id="1"><text>&lt;html&gt;Fur covers its body&lt;/html&gt;</text><image/><imagerefid/><audio/><audiorefid/></answer><answer id="2"><text>&lt;html&gt;It warms up in the armpits of bears&lt;/html&gt;</text><image/><imagerefid/><audio/><audiorefid/></answer><answer id="3"><text>&lt;html&gt;It makes a type of antifreeze&lt;/html&gt;</text><image/><imagerefid/><audio/><audiorefid/></answer><answer id="4"><text>&lt;html&gt;All of the above&lt;/html&gt;</text><image/><imagerefid/><audio/><audiorefid/></answer></answers><reward><text>&lt;html&gt;It makes a type of antifreeze. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The rock crawler produces a type of antifreeze that prevents its body fluids from freezing.
&lt;/html&gt;</text><image/><imagerefid/><audio/><audiorefid/></reward><credits/><rewardcredits/></quiz>